---
// src/pages/about.astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Mind is a Universe, author background, and site colophon."
>
  <article class="about-page">
    <header class="about-header">
      <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
      <p class="page-lead">
        A personal notebook for thoughts on software, design, and simplicity.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Hi there! I am a builder and tinkerer who enjoys clean code, thoughtful design,
        and making things that last. This site is my personal space to document what I learn,
        reflect on craft, and share occasional technical deep dives.
      </p>

      <h2>The Colophon</h2>
      <p>
        This website is built with an intentional emphasis on simplicity and performance:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Framework:</strong> Built statically with <a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Astro</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Styling:</strong> Pure native CSS custom properties defined in <code>tokens.css</code>. No CSS framework or preprocessor.</li>
        <li><strong>JavaScript:</strong> Zero client-side JavaScript shipped to readers, with the sole exception of the theme toggle script.</li>
        <li><strong>Typography:</strong> Native system font stacks tuned for high legibility across macOS, Windows, Linux, iOS, and Android.</li>
        <li><strong>Reading width:</strong> Text content is constrained to ~65 characters per line to guarantee comfortable reading rhythm.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Guiding Principles</h2>
      <blockquote>
        "Perfection is achieved, not when there is nothing more to add, but when there is nothing left to take away."
        <br />— Antoine de Saint-Exupéry
      </blockquote>

      <p>
        I believe the web should be fast, quiet, and respectful of the reader's attention.
        There are no tracking scripts, popups, or algorithmic feeds here. Just words, code,
        and ideas.
      </p>

      <h2>Stay Connected</h2>
      <p>
        The best way to follow new posts is by subscribing to the <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a> using your favorite feed reader (like NetNewsWire, Feedly, or Inoreader).
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .about-header {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .page-title {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .page-lead {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
